      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Page FOSS for Python reads PostScript (.ps), Encapsulated PostScript (.eps), and XML Paper Specification (.xps) files, and converts them to PDF. It also writes output in BMP (.bmp), JPEG (.jpeg), PNG (.png), and TIFF (.tiff) formats. It provides a model for building render documents with text and rendering them to raster images using the skia-python dependency."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "format:input.eps",
        "format:input.ps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "It reads and parses PostScript and Encapsulated PostScript documents using a full PostScript interpreter and extracts metadata."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "format:input.xps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "It reads and parses XML Paper Specification packages by walking fixed pages and print tickets through the parser and renderer."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:3",
      "text": "It creates and edits PostScript and XML Paper Specification documents from scratch using the canvas API or document builder, then saves them back to the source format."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:003",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:4",
      "text": "It builds page content programmatically with RenderModelBuilder, supporting paths, text, images, and a clip/state stack to produce a render document."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:003",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:5",
      "text": "It writes Portable Document Format output with PdfWriter, embedding fonts resolved through font resolver and font cache."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "dependency:skia-python",
        "format:output.bmp",
        "format:output.jpeg",
        "format:output.png",
        "format:output.tiff"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:6",
      "text": "It rasterizes PostScript content to bitmap, JPEG, PNG, or TIFF using the Skia backend by default, with a pure-Python fallback available for PS/EPS-to-image conversion only."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:004",
        "example:005",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.mcp"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:7",
      "text": "It exposes conversion tools such as ps_to_pdf, eps_metadata, and xps_to_pdf through the MCP module for FastMCP-based automation."
    },
