    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:058.paragraph"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "intro",
      "text": "The primary entry points are PsDocument and XpsDocument, which read, author, and convert PS/EPS and XPS content respectively; both delegate PDF output to PdfWriter and raster output to RasterRenderer, once page content has passed through the shared RenderModelBuilder / RenderDocument model."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.mcp",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.page",
      "text": "The aspose.page package provides the core render model types including RenderModelBuilder, RenderDocument, and RenderPage, which form the shared intermediate representation used by all format-specific readers and writers."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps.context.executioncontext",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps.dsc.dscmetadata",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps.font_cache.fontcache",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.ps.fonts.fontresolver"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.page.ps",
      "text": "The aspose.page.ps module supports reading and writing PostScript and EPS files through PsDocument, with font resolution handled by FontResolver and font metrics cached by FontCache, while DscMetadata captures document-level DSC comments."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps.editing.xpsdocumentbuilder",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps.package.xpspackage",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps.parser.xpsparser",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.xps.xpsdocument"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.page.xps",
      "text": "The aspose.page.xps module provides XpsDocument for loading and editing XPS documents, XpsDocumentBuilder for programmatic creation, XpsPackage for low-level package access, and XpsParser for parsing XPS package relationships."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf.pdfmetadata",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf.pdfwriter",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf.writer.rectwrapper"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.page.pdf",
      "text": "The aspose.page.pdf module exposes PdfWriter to serialize the shared render model into PDF 1.4 bytes, PdfMetadata for document info dictionary fields, and RectWrapper for bounding box coordinates."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image.raster_renderer.rasterrenderer",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image.raster_writer.defaultrasterwriter",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.image.skia_raster_writer.skiarasterwriter"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.page.image",
      "text": "The aspose.page.image module provides RasterRenderer for rendering the shared render model to raster surfaces, with DefaultRasterWriter and SkiaRasterWriter offering different backends for writing rendered output."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.mcp",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.mcp.create_server",
        "public_symbol:aspose.page.mcp.handlers",
